Services and external tools

  V1 talks to YouTube Music's web API (InnerTube), and fetches lyrics from
  Boidu (Better Lyrics) and LRCLIB. It fetches YouTube's player script at
  run time; that script is not bundled. V1 is not affiliated with or endorsed
  by YouTube, Google, Boidu or LRCLIB.

  Windows bundles FFmpeg and ffprobe from BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds; macOS builds them
  from the official FFmpeg 9.0.2 source archive at
  https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz. The macOS build disables external library autodetection, uses FFmpeg's
  internal libraries statically, and enables VideoToolbox, AudioToolbox and
  Secure Transport for native hardware video encoding, audio codecs and HTTPS.
  FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0. The
  macOS app includes its license, exact source archive and build configuration
  in Contents/Resources. V1 runs FFmpeg as a separate program and does not link
  to it. Windows installs its binaries in the ffmpeg folder with license text.
